  "output": "Here is the full performance analysis for this codebase:\n\n---\n\n## Performance Analysis: HR Policy Bot\n\n### CRITICAL Issues\n\n#### 1. Multiple `DatabaseManager` Instances Per Request (N+1 pattern)\n**`src/api/routes.py` lines 125, 140, 168, 179, 181**\n\nEach route handler instantiates a fresh `DatabaseManager()`. This bypasses any connection reuse and multiplies overhead under concurrency.\n\n```python\n# BEFORE (current — repeated in every handler)\ndb = DatabaseManager()\nqueries = await db.list_queries(limit=limit)\n\n# AFTER — singleton at module level\n_db: DatabaseManager | None = None\n\ndef get_db() -> DatabaseManager:\n    global _db\n    if _db is None:\n        _db = DatabaseManager()\n    return _db\n\n# Then in each handler:\nqueries = await get_db().list_queries(limit=limit)\n```\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Unbounded WebSocket Connection Cache (memory leak)\n**`src/api/websocket.py` lines 29, 34, 40**\n\n`_connections: dict[str, WebSocket]` grows forever. Clients that abnormally disconnect are never evicted, so every query_id ever used stays in memory indefinitely.\n\n```python\n# AFTER — add max-size guard and cleanup\nMAX_CONNECTIONS = 500\n\nasync def connect(self, query_id: str, websocket: WebSocket) -> None:\n    if len(self._connections) >= MAX_CONNECTIONS:\n        # evict oldest entry\n        oldest = next(iter(self._connections))\n        del self._connections[oldest]\n    await websocket.accept()\n    self._connections[query_id] = websocket\n```\n\n---\n\n### MODERATE Issues\n\n#### 3. Policy Registry Loaded 8× on Startup (missing cache)\n**`src/agents/specialist.py` lines 70, 72–75**\n\nEach of the 8 specialist agents opens and JSON-parses `policy_registry.json` independently on `__init__`.\n\n```python\n# BEFORE — in _load_instruments()\nwith open(_REGISTRY_PATH) as f:\n    registry = json.load(f)   # called 8 times\n\n# AFTER — module-level cache\n_registry_cache: list[dict] | None = None\n\ndef _get_registry() -> list[dict]:\n    global _registry_cache\n    if _registry_cache is None:\n        with open(_REGISTRY_PATH) as f:\n            _registry_cache = json.load(f)\n    return _registry_cache\n\ndef _load_instruments(self, agent_id: str) -> list[dict]:\n    return [r for r in _get_registry() if agent_id in r[\"agent_ids\"]]\n```\n\n---\n\n#### 4. Health Check Makes Two Separate COUNT Queries (N+1)\n**`src/api/routes.py` lines 94–99**\n\n```python\n# BEFORE — two round-trips\nasync with db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM queries\") as cur: ...\nasync with db.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM feedback\") as cur: ...\n\n# AFTER — single query\nasync with db.execute(\n    \"SELECT (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM queries), (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM feedback)\"\n) as cur:\n    query_count, feedback_count = await cur.fetchone()\n```\n\n---\n\n#### 5. Unbounded Domain Tracking in Fetch Engine (memory leak)\n**`src/fetch/engine.py` lines 43–46, 84**\n\n`_domain_semaphores` and `_domain_last_request` dicts grow with every unique domain encountered and are never cleaned up. Add periodic eviction:\n\n```python\nasync def _evict_stale_domains(self, max_age_s: float = 86400.0) -> None:\n    now = time.monotonic()\n    stale = [d for d, t in self._domain_last_request.items() if now - t > max_age_s]\n    for d in stale:\n        self._domain_last_request.pop(d, None)\n        self._domain_semaphores.pop(d, None)\n```\n\nCall this during `close()` or on a periodic timer.\n\n---\n\n#### 6. No Response Caching for Identical Queries (missing cache)\n**`src/api/websocket.py` lines 170–174**\n\nIdentical questions trigger full re-processing (8 agent fetches + 8 LLM calls). A simple text-hash cache with a 24h TTL would eliminate this:\n\n```python\nimport hashlib, time\n\n_response_cache: dict[str, tuple[float, OrchestratorResponse]] = {}\nCACHE_TTL = 86400  # 24h\n\ndef _cache_key(query_text: str) -> str:\n    return hashlib.sha256(query_text.strip().lower().encode()).hexdigest()\n\n# Before processing:\nkey = _cache_key(query_text)\nif key in _response_cache:\n    ts, cached = _response_cache[key]\n    if time.time() - ts < CACHE_TTL:\n        return cached  # skip all agent calls\n\n# After processing:\n_response_cache[key] = (time.time(), response)\n```\n\n---\n\n### LOW Issues\n\n| Issue | File | Lines | Fix |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `querySelector` repeated inside rapid update loops | `static/js/app.js` | 145, 163, 173, 186 | Cache DOM refs in module scope |\n| Full raw LLM output (5–10 KB) stored on JSON parse error | `src/agents/specialist.py` | 163–174 | Truncate `raw` to 1 KB |\n| Citation list fully cleared and rebuilt each render | `static/js/app.js` | 344–365 | Diff against existing list or use a document fragment |\n| SQLite cache has no size cap — grows unbounded | `src/fetch/cache.py` | 72–86 | Add `PRAGMA page_count` check or periodic `VACUUM` |\n| `httpx.AsyncClient` may not close on unclean shutdown | `src/fetch/engine.py` | 162–164 | Wrap fetch engine startup in `try/finally` in lifespan |\n\n---\n\n### Priority Summary\n\n| Priority | Action | Expected Impact |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Singleton `DatabaseManager` | Eliminates redundant SQLite init on every request |\n| 2 | WebSocket connection TTL/cap | Prevents memory growth over hours of uptime |\n| 3 | Module-level registry cache | Removes 7 redundant file reads at startup |\n| 4 | Combined health-check query | Halves DB round-trips on `/health` |\n| 5 | Query-level LLM response cache | Eliminates repeat LLM calls for identical questions |\n| 6 | Domain tracking eviction | Prevents slow memory leak in long-running deployments |\n\nThe two most impactful fixes right now are **#1** (DB manager singleton) and **#2** (WebSocket connection cap), as both are correctness issues that worsen over time, not just performance concerns.\n",
